    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Religious habit",
      "publisher": "Wikipedia",
      "author": null,
      "published_at": null,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=3660658",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T14:56:05.930Z",
      "sha256": "2940065bfc9ca2366d198a7979250d779bcc8bf63760098ae96445fff14219f0",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "A religious habit is a distinctive set of clothing worn by members of a religious order or a religious congregation.",
        "Traditionally, some plain garb recognizable as a religious habit has also been worn by those leading the hermits and anchorites, although in their case without conformity to a particular uniform style.",
        "Uniformity and distinctiveness by order or congregation often evolved and changed over time.",
        "Interpretation of terms for clothes in religious rules could change over centuries.",
        "Furthermore, every time new communities gained importance in a cultural area the need for visual separation increased for new as well as old communities.",
        "Thus, modern habits are rooted in historic forms, but do not necessarily resemble them in cut, color, material, detail or use.",
        "In monastic orders of the Catholic and Anglican churches, the habit often consists of a tunic covered by a scapular and a cowl, with a hood for monks or friars and a veil for nuns.",
        "Canon Law requires only that the garb of their members be in some way identifiable so that the person may serve as a witness of the Evangelical counsels.",
        "In many orders or congregations,the beginning of the novitiate is marked by the ceremony of investiture, in which the canditate is accepted as a novice and then clothed in the community's habit by the superior of the community.",
        "In some cases the novice's habit will be somewhat different from the customary habit: for instance, in certain communities it is common for the female novices to wear a white veil while professed sisters wear black.",
        "Carthusian novices wear a black cloak over their white tunics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "title": "Habit",
      "publisher": "Wikipedia",
      "author": null,
      "published_at": null,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=13149599",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T14:56:05.930Z",
      "sha256": "59517c9baa4674dc2ce19dfdafe781d7fee0a731d2b56c4136a946334163287b",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "A habit (or wont, the original word in English) is a routine of behavior that is repeated regularly and tends to occur subconsciously.",
        "A 2002 daily experience study by habit researcher Wendy Wood and her colleagues found that approximately 43% of daily behaviors are performed out of habit.",
        "New behaviours can become automatic through the process of habit formation.",
        "Old habits are hard to break and new habits are hard to form because the behavioural patterns that humans repeat become imprinted in neural pathways, but it is possible to form new habits through repetition.",
        "When behaviors are repeated in a consistent context, there is an incremental increase in the link between the context and the action.",
        "This increases the automaticity of the behavior in that context.",
        "Features of an automatic behavior are all or some of: efficiency, lack of awareness, unintentionality, and uncontrollability."
      ]
    },
